  38:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c **** 
  39:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c **** /**
  40:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * @defgroup httpd HTTP server
  41:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * @ingroup apps
  42:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  43:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * This httpd supports for a
  44:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * rudimentary server-side-include facility which will replace tags of the form
  45:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * <!--#tag--> in any file whose extension is .shtml, .shtm or .ssi with
  46:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * strings provided by an include handler whose pointer is provided to the
  47:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * module via function http_set_ssi_handler().
  48:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * Additionally, a simple common
  49:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * gateway interface (CGI) handling mechanism has been added to allow clients
  50:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * to hook functions to particular request URIs.
  51:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  52:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * To enable SSI support, define label LWIP_HTTPD_SSI in lwipopts.h.
  53:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * To enable CGI support, define label LWIP_HTTPD_CGI in lwipopts.h.
  54:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  55:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * By default, the server assumes that HTTP headers are already present in
  56:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * each file stored in the file system.  By defining LWIP_HTTPD_DYNAMIC_HEADERS in
  57:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * lwipopts.h, this behavior can be changed such that the server inserts the
  58:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * headers automatically based on the extension of the file being served.  If
  59:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * this mode is used, be careful to ensure that the file system image used
  60:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * does not already contain the header information.
  61:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  62:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * File system images without headers can be created using the makefsfile
  63:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * tool with the -h command line option.
  64:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  65:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  66:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * Notes about valid SSI tags
  67:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * --------------------------
  68:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  69:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * The following assumptions are made about tags used in SSI markers:
  70:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  71:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * 1. No tag may contain '-' or whitespace characters within the tag name.
  72:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * 2. Whitespace is allowed between the tag leadin "<!--#" and the start of
  73:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *    the tag name and between the tag name and the leadout string "-->".
  74:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * 3. The maximum tag name length is LWIP_HTTPD_MAX_TAG_NAME_LEN, currently 8 characters.
  75:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  76:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * Notes on CGI usage
  77:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * ------------------
  78:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  79:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * The simple CGI support offered here works with GET method requests only
  80:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * and can handle up to 16 parameters encoded into the URI. The handler
  81:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * function may not write directly to the HTTP output but must return a
  82:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * filename that the HTTP server will send to the browser as a response to
  83:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * the incoming CGI request.
  84:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  85:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  86:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  *
  87:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * The list of supported file types is quite short, so if makefsdata complains
  88:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * about an unknown extension, make sure to add it (and its doctype) to
  89:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  * the 'g_psHTTPHeaders' list.
  90:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c ****  */
  91:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c **** #include "lwip/init.h"
  92:./lwip-2.1.2/src/apps/http/httpd.c **** #include "lwip/apps/httpd.h"
